From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:58:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: drop the empty COMPAT_ARCH_DLINFO of binfmt_elf32.c

asm/elf.h defines COMPAT_ARCH_DLINFO for AArch32 (AT_SYSINFO_EHDR with
COMPAT_VDSO, empty otherwise) and is included by compat_binfmt_elf.c after
the empty definition in binfmt_elf32.c, which only caused a "redefined"
warning with COMPAT_VDSO=y. The asm/elf.h one was already in effect.
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/binfmt_elf32.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/binfmt_elf32.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/binfmt_elf32.c
@@ -17,7 +17,6 @@
 	set_thread_flag(TIF_32BIT);					\
 })
 
-#define COMPAT_ARCH_DLINFO
 #define COMPAT_ELF_HWCAP		(a32_elf_hwcap)
 #define COMPAT_ELF_HWCAP2		(a32_elf_hwcap2)
 
